# ============================================================================
# annotate landing — Night Desk direction — HERO, feedback-to-fix flow (16:10)
# Model: nano banana (gemini / gemini-2.5-flash-image) — pinned below.
# AI-GENERATED MEDIA: disclose as AI-generated when published.
# Run: generate-media-prompt design/landing/prompts/night-desk/hero-sdlc.media.prompt
# Replaces the hero-realistic pricing-page shot (fake prices, garbled glyphs).
# Text budget: 6 short strings. No prices, no third-party logos.
# ============================================================================
schema: '0.4'

id: annotate-landing-nightdesk-hero-sdlc
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Polished dark product illustration, 16:10, the whole scene (browser plus cards) large, centered, and filling about 80 percent of the frame width and height, with generous but even margins; keep everything away from the top and bottom 8 percent of the frame, near-black background with one
    soft warm ember glow. On the left, a flat browser window (ONE single title bar with exactly three small GRAY dots, never red, yellow or green, followed directly by the page content; no second toolbar, no second row of dots, no address bar) showing a generic dark web app page: a
    sidebar of plain gray bars, a top nav of gray bars, a grid of raised dark
    cards filled with abstract gray placeholder lines and small chart shapes,
    NO readable text on the page except one small button labelled "Export" in
    the top right. That "Export" button is surrounded by a crisp glowing
    ember-orange ring with a small orange pin marker on its corner. A thin
    luminous orange connector line runs from the ring to a comment thread
    card to the right of the browser, outside the window. The card is a dark
    raised panel with hairline gray border and exactly two comments, each with
    a plain muted orange-tinted circle avatar (no letters, no faces, no blue or green): first comment text
    "Export button is cut off on mobile", second comment (indented reply)
    "Reproduced. Filing it.". Below the thread card a thin orange arrow flows
    down to a compact ticket card with a small orange check icon and the text
    "Ticket created". From the ticket card another thin orange arrow flows to
    a compact terminal-style agent card with a monospaced font and two lines:
    "agent: on it" and "patch ready" (the second line with a small
    orange check). The ONLY text in the whole image is exactly these strings:
    Export · Export button is cut off on mobile · Reproduced. Filing it. ·
    Ticket created · agent: on it · patch ready. Clean
    Inter-style grotesque sans for UI text, large type, each string in a single line where possible, crisp, correctly spelled, high
    contrast, large enough to read, no duplicated or warped text. Calm,
    precise, generous negative space, left-to-right flow.
  negative: garbled glyphs, pseudo-letters, misspelled words, duplicated text,
    prices, dollar signs, currency, any real brand name or logo (Jira, Notion,
    ClickUp, Asana), URLs, hex codes, hash symbols, photographic people or
    faces, initials in avatars, extra paragraphs of text, blue or green glow,
    light theme, rainbow gradients, lens flares, watermark
  style: dark-native flat UI illustration, vector-sharp, single warm ember
    accent #E8913F, soft bloom, window dots gray not red/yellow/green, generous negative space

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1248
    height: 832
    aspect_ratio: '3:2'  # native; center-crop to 16:10 (1248x780) in post

requirements:
  subject: browser page with ringed element, connected comment thread, ticket card, agent terminal card
  composition: left-to-right flow; browser left, thread card right, ticket and agent cards stacked/flowing below or beyond
  palette: near-black canvas, dark raised surfaces, single ember accent #E8913F
  dont:
    - prices, brand logos, URLs, extra text, faces

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  required_pass:
    - text_legibility
    - no_prices_or_logos
  criteria:
    text_legibility:
      weight: 3
      description: Every string matches the manifest exactly, crisp, no garbled glyphs
      fail_signals:
        - pseudo-letters or warped words
        - misspellings or duplicated strings
        - extra readable text beyond the manifest
    no_prices_or_logos:
      weight: 2
      description: No prices, currency, third-party logos or fake brand names
      fail_signals:
        - dollar signs or numbers that look like prices
        - recognizable Jira/Notion/ClickUp/Asana marks
    accent_colour:
      weight: 2
      description: Single warm orange (~#E8913F) accent on near-black, soft glow
      fail_signals:
        - second glow hue
        - light theme
    composition:
      weight: 3
      description: Ring+pin on element, connector to thread, flow arrows to ticket then agent card; clear left-to-right story
      fail_signals:
        - connector or arrows missing/detached
        - cluttered or overlapping cards
  reject_if:
    - garbled or misspelled text
    - price or currency symbol
    - third-party logo
    - photographic face

tags: [marketing, landing-hero, annotate, ai-generated]
product_targets: [annotate.therobotlives.com]
